  "[silence] (to O-lan) Wang Lung says nothing.",
  "O-lan (to Wang Lung): \"Why do you say that? I am not a pig. I eat my fill every day. And the children eat their fill, too. It is not I who am hungry now.\"",
  "[says] O-lan asks if it is because the land does not bear enough grain.",
  "O-lan (to Wang Lung): \"Is it that the land does not bear enough grain? Or is it that you do not till it well?\"",
